Patches that still describe a real problem on this board but do not yet
apply to the current branch.

patch_trees() in tools/build_lineage.sh walks patches/ and fails the whole
post-sync step on the first patch it cannot apply -- correctly, since a
patch that silently does not apply is worse than none. So a patch waiting
to be ported lives here instead, where the finder does not look, and moves
back to patches/ once it applies.

Nothing here is optional. Each file carries its own reasoning in the
commit message; read that before deciding it can be dropped.
